Based on the documentation for nginx: NGINX Enterprise Security Headers (HSTS, CSP, X-Frame) (Module 011)

### NGINX Enterprise Security Headers (HSTS, CSP, X-Frame) - Configuration Guide 011

Add security headers via add_header: Strict-Transport-Security 'max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains', X-Content-Type-Options nosniff, X-Frame-Options DENY, and Content-Security-Policy.

#### Production NGINX Directives #011
In edge routing configuration 011, upstream connectivity and security isolation are prioritized.

```nginx
# NGINX configuration block for nginx_security_headers_hsts #011
upstream backend_cluster_011 {
    least_conn;
    server 10.0.11.10:8080 max_fails=3 fail_timeout=10s;
    server 10.0.11.11:8080 max_fails=3 fail_timeout=10s;
    keepalive 32;
}

server {
    listen 443 ssl http2;
    server_name service-011.enterprise.internal;
    ssl_certificate /etc/nginx/ssl/service-011.crt;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/ssl/service-011.key;

    location /api/v1/ {
        proxy_pass http://backend_cluster_011;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Connection "";
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_read_timeout 41s;
    }
}
```.

